      "role": "user",
      "content": "neurodisruption? okay, but what i mean is, it doesn't feel like a \"disturbance\" or like my vision is just glitching. it feels like the colors are actually tied to the events. like, if there's a huge red mass in my periphery, i know i need to move out of the way or something bad is going to happen within seconds. it's too consistent to be a random hallucination. could the particle exposure have actually altered my neural pathways to detect something the rest of us just can't see? like maybe a way to perceive probability or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
